# elect.sync as an instruction guard: the elected lane of warp 0
# stores 4 B, the elected lane of each of the 4 warps 8 B, every other
# lane 2 B, and lane 0 stores 4 B only if it is its warp's elected
# lane, which is unspecified: 284 B plus a bound of 4.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/elect.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_elect
CHECK: block size: 128 threads, 4 warps (128x1x1 from .reqntid)
CHECK: global bytes: load 4 B, store <= 18 B
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 512 B, store <= 288 B
